    "created_at": "2018-08-29T00:06:56Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-08-29T00:06:56Z",
    "body": "> But then, legend should allow list-item, right?\r\n\r\nWell, maybe :-) It will require some work in Gecko to get the numbering correct in that case, so we might want to disallow it for that reason.  For example, what should numbering be for:\r\n```html\r\n<style>\r\nol { -webkit-appearance: fieldset; border: 1px solid; }\r\nol > * { display:list-item }\r\n</style>\r\n\r\n<ol start=\"5\">\r\n  <div>A</div>\r\n  <legend>B</legend>\r\n  <div>C</div>\r\n</ol>\r\n```\r\n\r\nCurrently, we get:\r\n```\r\n0. B\r\n5. A\r\n6. C\r\n```\r\nwhich seems like a not very useful result. I've posted a few examples of our fieldset box tree in https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/3934#issuecomment-416777483. I suspect that getting the numbering to be \"6 5 7\" above would require some non-trivial work in Gecko.  So yeah, I think I'd prefer to exclude `list-item` for legends for that reason. It doesn't seem like a very useful use case anyway.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
